        "original_id": "0982fd49-6b50-552b-abbe-8218922917f4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Miami Dolphins, Kansas City Chiefs, New York Jets\n- People: Adam Gase, Andy Reid, John Dorsey\n- Topics: 2016 NFL seasons, playoff berth, winning record, coaching and management tenures\n\nFacts:\n- The 2016 Miami Dolphins season was the franchise's first season under head coach Adam Gase.\n- In Week 15 of the 2016 season, the Miami Dolphins clinched a winning record for the first time since 2008 with a win over the New York Jets.\n- The Miami Dolphins clinched a playoff berth the following week in the 2016 season.\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was the team's fourth season under head coach Andy Reid.\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was the fourth and final season under general manager John Dorsey.\n- John Dorsey was fired by the Kansas City Chiefs on June 22, 2017.",
