        "original_id": "aa431c8c-3fac-5b06-a9d4-b6e826d67bc8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: Miami Dolphins, Kansas City Chiefs, New York Jets, Denver Broncos\n- People: Andy Reid, John Dorsey\n- Seasons: 2016 Miami Dolphins season, 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season\n- Organizations: National Football League\n- Roles: head coach, general manager\n\nFacts:\n- The 2016 Kansas City Chiefs season was the franchise's 47th season in the National Football League and its 57th season overall.\n- Andy Reid served his fourth season as head coach of the Kansas City Chiefs in 2016.\n- John Dorsey served his fourth and final season as general manager of the Kansas City Chiefs in 2016.\n- The Miami Dolphins clinched a winning record in Week 15 of the 2016 season with a win over the New York Jets, their first winning record since 2008.\n- The Miami Dolphins clinched a playoff berth the following week after the Kansas City Chiefs defeated the Denver Broncos.\n- John Dorsey was fired by the Kansas City Chiefs on June 22, 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
